  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Mole negro starts with "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "toasting"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "toasting"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " dried chillies until they blister, then grinding them into a paste that forms the sauce base. A small amount of dark chocolate added at the end rounds the heat and gives the sauce its characteristic depth. "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "deglazing"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "Deglazing"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " the pan after frying the paste lifts the colour and body into the finished sauce."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Tip: do not skip charring the onion and garlic directly in a dry pan. That burnt edge is part of the flavour."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
